From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nivogli <224451320+nivogli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 17:02:09 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Cap the Metal draws encoded per indirect-count command

MoltenVK encodes maxDrawCount Metal indirect draws on the CPU for every
vkCmdDraw[Indexed]IndirectCount and zeroes the unused ones on the GPU. An
application that passes a maxDrawCount far above its real counts pays for
every one of them. Encode at most a cap of 256 draws per command instead.

The cap corrects itself. A conversion kernel counts commands whose real
count exceeded their cap, and each new truncation seen at encode time
doubles the cap, which is never lowered. One stderr line records a raise.

Adopted from https://github.com/nivogli/MoltenVK commits
08e692dc7bf68b1f40a852fa203ce329beb893ca,
5546b02879570800600580ea5ad54166f931eec4,
96793f1de5fd898a8e4ad3b7d7b52f23b8bac483 and the needed part of
d496ec14f57c12f14e75d9e057b3667d9f466ade.

Modifications:
- Those commits lowered _drawCount in setContent(), at record time, so
  command buffers submitted again kept dropping draws and a raised cap
  never reached them. _drawCount now keeps the application's maxDrawCount;
  each encode path reads the cap once into a local count and uses that
  count for every buffer size and dispatch, so nothing is sized by a
  different value than the dispatch writing it, also if the cap rises
  between calls. The triangle-fan path receives the count as an argument.
- A prefilled command buffer keeps the cap of its encode for that one
  submission. MoltenVK clears it on submit and later submissions encode
  again with the current cap. Immediate encoding behaves the same.
- Self-correction is always on with the cap, and the only switch is
  MVK_PERF_ICOUNT_MAX_DRAWS. MVK_PERF_ICOUNT_STATS, histograms, summary
  prints and all counters except truncation are removed. The decay of
  34f8bc8644963f90bac0b70b14b07fac30cae2c4 is dropped; it was dead after
  96793f1d. No new file: the helpers live in MVKCmdDraw.mm.
- The upper limit on the cap is removed, because a real count above it
  would have dropped draws forever.
- The counter is process-wide. A device other than the first gets no cap
  rather than a counter bound to the wrong device.

Residual: the first time a real count exceeds the cap, draws can be
missing until the raise takes effect, for a few frames if it needs more
than one doubling. MVK_PERF_ICOUNT_MAX_DRAWS=0 disables the cap.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
